Nim.

How to Play:
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Press button 1 to start the game.
During your turn, use buttons 1 and 2 to select the number of matches to remove.
Press button 1 to confirm your move.
Wait for the LED display to update and show the current game status.
Wait for the computer's turn.
Repeat steps 2-5 until the game ends.
The winner (Player or Computer) will be displayed on the LED display.
Game Progress:
The game progress is displayed on the LED display and serial monitor. Each turn shows:

Removal Count: Number of matches removed in the current turn.
Player Turn: Indicates whether it's the human player's or computer's turn.
Remaining Matches: Number of matches remaining in the pile.
Memory Management:
The game logs are stored in dynamic memory using malloc and realloc functions. Memory is allocated dynamically to accommodate the growing number of game logs as the game progresses.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Overview of Methods:

startMatch():

This method initiates the game by waiting for the start button press.
 It continuously checks for button press until the start button is pressed.
 Used at the beginning of the game to start the match.

determineFirstPlayer():
 Determines the first player randomly.
 Generates a random number and assigns 'p' for player or 'c' for computer based on the result.
 Used to decide which player starts the game.

ISR(PCINT1_vect):

Interrupt Service Routine for handling button presses.
 Detects button presses and adjusts the game state accordingly.
 Used to handle player inputs during the game.

initializeGame():

 Initializes the game components and sets up the environment.
 Initializes USART, display, ADC, and enables buttons. Allocates memory for game logs.
 Called at the beginning of the program to set up the game environment.

handleMatchUpdate(int count):

 Updates the match count and checks for game completion.
 Subtracts the count from remaining matches and ensures it doesn't go below 1.
 Used to update the match count during each turn.

logProgress(int turn, char player, int removed, int remaining):

 Logs the progress of each turn in the game.
 Stores the turn number, player, number of matches removed, and remaining matches in the game logs array.
 Used to record the progress of the game for analysis or debugging purposes.

showWinner(char winner):

 Displays the winner of the game on the LED display.
 Displays 'GOOD' if the player wins and 'LOSS' if the computer wins.
 Called at the end of the game to announce the winner.

displayCurrentStatus():

 Displays the current game status on the LED display.
 Writes the removal count, player turn, and remaining matches 
 to the LED display.
 Used to show the current game status during each turn.
updateDisplay():

Updates the LED display with the current game status.
 Writes the removal count, player turn, and remaining matches to the LED display.
Called after each turn to update the display with the latest game status.

main():
Functionality: Initializes the game, enables interrupts, and enters the game loop. Handles player turns and game progression.
Usage: Executes the game logic and controls the flow of the program.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Enjoy!